  "description": "ExpertPdf HTML to PDF Converter is a .NET library that converts web pages, HTML strings and HTML files to PDF documents and images. It renders the HTML like a browser, with a choice of rendering engines, and gives you full control over the PDF: page settings, headers and footers, bookmarks, links, security, PDF/A, tagged PDF and electronic invoices.\n\nThis package contains the library for .NET Framework 4.6.1 to 4.8.1, .NET Core 2.0+ and .NET 5 to .NET 11 (through .NET Standard 2.0). It is the build for 64-bit (x64) applications; for x86 and AnyCPU applications use ExpertPdf.HtmlToPdf.NetCore.\n\nFeatures\n- Convert web pages (URLs), HTML strings and HTML files to PDF documents, and to images\n- Three rendering engines: WebKit (built in), Blink and Chromium (separate engine packages) with full support for HTML5, CSS3, web fonts and modern JavaScript\n- Page size, orientation, margins, fit width, page breaks control (CSS page-break, keep together), repeated table headers\n- Headers and footers with HTML content and page numbering\n- Automatic bookmarks, table of contents, live internal and external links\n- Tagged (accessible) PDF / PDF/UA, PDF/A-1b, PDF/A-2b, PDF/A-3b, PDF/A-3u, PDF/A-3a and PDF/X-1a\n- ZUGFeRD 2.x / Factur-X electronic invoices and associated files (PDF/A-3)\n- Security: user and owner passwords, print / copy / edit permissions, 40, 128 and 256 bit encryption; digital signatures\n- Authentication, cookies, HTTP headers and POST data; select or exclude page elements; JavaScript delay and conversion triggered from JavaScript\n- Add text, images, shapes and more HTML to the generated PDF; merge with existing PDF documents\n- Thread safe: convert in parallel in web applications and services\n\nRendering engines\n- WebKit - built in, the default engine.\n- Blink (Chromium 148) - install ExpertPdf.HtmlToPdf.NetCore.Blink.x64; .NET Framework 4.6.1+ and .NET Core / .NET 5+.\n- Chromium (Chromium 154) - install ExpertPdf.HtmlToPdf.NetCore.Chromium.Windows.x64; Windows; runs in its own process.",
